From 5a645c126c3da5bb712506613f9c10697579f94d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:11:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban sync heal: last lifecycle move decides the
 park, skip bad rows, warn once

Follow-ups from the PR1358 review (t_01a1cf5a17c81aae):

- _parked_status now takes the card's last lifecycle move since the run's park
  event. The triage sweeps (agent_block_escalated, ask_rechecked,
  supervisor_escalated) count as leaving the park, and a later park event (the
  wake invariant's scheduled -> blocked) lands that park.
- Events are ordered by origin time: second, then the uid's UUIDv7
  millisecond, then local id. A same-second unblock that arrived before its
  block is no longer missed.
- A malformed event payload reads as no payload (Python parse in
  _parked_status, CASE json_valid in the once-gate). Each card heals in its own
  try, so one failing card never aborts the round.
- The once-gate "still reads running after one heal" warning logs once per
  (task, run) per process.
- A restored blocked park takes block_kind and human_request from its own
  event. A restored scheduled park clears human_request, as schedule_task does.
  The wake rows are not task columns, so a stale copy can't touch them.
- _stale_lifecycle docstring: the claim_lock guard covers only the
  terminal-replica branch.

Tests: 10 new or tightened in test_kanban_sync_running_heal.py. They fail on
the main module and pass here (23/23). All 45 test_kanban_sync*.py files pass
(684 tests).
